              </div>
              <div class="project-context">IPC contribution · anisotropic friction</div>
              <div class="project-card-body">
                <div class="project-gallery" role="group" aria-label="ipc-toolkit FEM contact simulation visualization">
                  <figure>
                    <button type="button" class="job-gallery-preview-link" data-image-preview-open data-image-preview-src="papers/ipc-toolkit/images/ipc-toolkit-fem-mesh.png" data-image-preview-alt="3D FEM mesh visualization from IPC Toolkit contact simulation with triangular surface elements" data-image-preview-caption="IPC contact mesh during friction simulation." aria-label="View full-size ipc-toolkit FEM mesh visualization">
                      <img src="papers/ipc-toolkit/images/ipc-toolkit-fem-mesh.png" alt="" width="584" height="332" loading="lazy" decoding="async" aria-hidden="true" />
                      <span class="job-gallery-preview-hint" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fas fa-expand"></i></span>
                    </button>
                    <figcaption>IPC contact mesh during friction simulation</figcaption>
                  </figure>
                </div>
                <div class="project-card-copy">
                  <div class="project-impact">Contribution to <a href="https://github.com/ipc-sim/ipc-toolkit/pull/210" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">anisotropic friction</a> work in the <a href="https://github.com/ipc-sim/ipc-toolkit" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPC Toolkit</a>. The work extends contact friction handling in a serious simulation codebase, across the C++/Eigen core, Python <code>ipctk</code> bindings, notebooks, and tests.</div>
                  <div class="project-tags">
                    <span class="project-tag">C++</span><span class="project-tag">Eigen</span><span class="project-tag">Python</span><span class="project-tag">Simulation</span><span class="project-tag">Friction</span>
